1
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:16,000
When every college turned them down. . . they made one up.

2
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Accepted is a comedy film directed by Steve Pink.

3
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:36,000
A high school slacker who's rejected by every school he applies to opts to create his own institution of higher
learning, the South Harmon Institute of Technology, on a rundown piece of property near his hometown.

4
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Bartleby Gaines, played by Justin Long.

5
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Sherman Schrader, played by Jonah Hill.

6
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Monica Moreland, played by Blake Lively.

7
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:16,000
Glen, played by Adam Herschman.

8
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:26,000
Hands, played by Columbus Short.

9
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Rory, played by Maria Thayer.

10
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:46,000
Accepted is a 2006 American comedy film directed by
Steve Pink, marking his directorial debut.

11
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:56,000
The screenplay was written by Adam Cooper, Bill Collage, and Mark Perez.

12
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
The film stars Justin Long, Blake Lively, Anthony
Heald and Lewis Black in lead roles.

13
01:07:10,000 --> 01:07:16,000
The plot follows Bartleby Gaines, a high school graduate who, after being rejected by every college he applies to, concocts a
plan to create a fake university with his friends to convince his parents he's moving forward with his education.

14
01:12:20,000 --> 01:12:26,000
As more students, also rejected from other schools, mistakenly apply to the fictional South Harmon Institute of
Technology (S.H.I.T.), Bartleby and his friends decide to run the school as if it were a real institution.

15
01:17:30,000 --> 01:17:36,000
The film was released on August 18, 2006, and
received mixed reviews from critics.

16
01:22:40,000 --> 01:22:46,000
The film explores themes of straitjacket ,
college, fraud, girlfriend, university.

17
01:27:50,000 --> 01:27:56,000
The tone is lighthearted.
